  "body": "Currently, the [advised way to feature-detect support for `new Worker({type: \"module\"})`](https://gist.github.com/developit/5b09dc86c644d76f8fbd8abe294440f2) is to create an options object and see if the `.type` property gets accessed by the constructor with a getter:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nlet supportsModuleWorker = false;\r\nconst options = {\r\n  get type() {\r\n    supportsModuleWorker = true\r\n  }\r\n};\r\nnew Worker(\"data:,\", options).terminate();\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat seems fairly convoluted. I propose adding `type` property to module instances:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst w = new Worker(\"data:,\", {type: \"module\"})\r\nconst supportsModuleWorker = \"type\" in w;\r\nw.terminate();\r\n```",
